1. She is British and emphasizes British tea culture. (Verbatim: "I'm British. It is English breakfast. English breakfast is THE tea.")
2. Her favorite tea brand is Yorkshire Tea, which she considers superior. (Verbatim: "Specifically, I use Yorkshire tea." / "Favorite tea band anything other than Yorkshire is blasphemy.")
3. She takes her tea with one teaspoon of sugar and milk, preferring a lighter color for more milk. (Verbatim: "I have one teaspoon of sugar, and a bit of milk." / "I like it kind of like, on the lighter side because I really like milk.")
4. She once babysat for a Chinese family and had a cultural misunderstanding about being offered hot water. (Verbatim: "This was the Chinese family I used to um do babysitting for... I got given a cup of hot water like like just hot boiling water and I was like what am I supposed to do with this cup of hot water.")
5. She has a habit of offering tea to guests, reflecting a British cultural norm. (Verbatim: "Fun fact, if you go to England, it really is traditional to always offer a cup of tea if someone comes to visit you.")
6. She has had digestive issues she suspects are from old butter kept since April. (Verbatim: "I think it's my butter because I've had it since like April and it's September.")
7. She enjoys stroopwafels and eats them by placing them on top of a hot mug of tea to melt. (Verbatim: "A waffle on top. A stroopwafel or whatever it's called... the heat from the tea shall melt the waffle.")
8. She has a messy sleeping pattern and often sleeps only 3–4 hours. (Verbatim: "I had... About four. No, like three-something.")
9. She wants to create a VTuber flag and has been practicing her signature. (Verbatim: "I want a flag... I've been working on my signature.")
10. She once considered doing a thigh-squishing challenge stream but jokes her thighs aren’t strong enough. (Verbatim: "I wanna see what level of fruit I can squish... I don't... my thighs are not strong enough.") [end of text]



1. She considers herself clumsy and has been called "cursed" by her parents because things she touches break. (Verbatim: "everything you touch breaks and i'm like oh my cursed like")
2. She lives in a one-bedroom flat in the UK and feels she doesn’t deserve such a nice place, describing it as too fancy and mold-free. (Verbatim: "i shouldn't be living in such a nice place... there's not a speck of mold it's kind of wild")
3. She moved into her current residence when she became a developer and plans to downgrade her living situation in the future. (Verbatim: "i moved into this place when when i became a developer... the plan is to move and downgrade probably by quite a bit")
