10. She plans to announce a major personal investment or project around her debut anniversary in March, which will be the most expensive thing she’s ever invested in. (Verbatim: "for next year round march for my birthday i'm gonna announce what it is... the most expensive thing i've ever invested in") [end of text]



1. She experienced nepotism in an academic setting, where a teacher's son's girlfriend was chosen over her despite equal or better work. (Verbatim: "they picked her because she was the teacher's son's girlfriend... i was like okay i don't like this i'd like to go do science instead")

2. She values hard work and fairness, expressing disappointment in systems where connections matter more than merit. (Verbatim: "i just want to work hard make friends and have a good time... i wish the world was simply you know work hard be rewarded")

3. She strongly dislikes networking and the idea of using people for personal gain, finding it morally repulsive. (Verbatim: "i really really hate the idea of like... networking what bleh bleh people are not to be used")

4. She has a negative view of favoritism, especially in educational environments, recalling a college teacher who focused only on certain students. (Verbatim: "oh my gosh i had that in english college... she literally only focused on like these three students and the rest of us were treated like literal trash")

5. She identifies as a middle child and relates to the associated traits such as independence and feelings of alienation. (Verbatim: "i could tell i was middle child because you're also middle child and we share the same energy")

6. She describes herself as having "middle child energy," including being independent, less family-oriented, and feeling forgotten. (Verbatim: "strong sense of independence yeah less family orientated yo feelings of alienation yo")

7. She became a VTuber partly as a way to combat loneliness and build meaningful friendships online. (Verbatim: "it makes me so happy to have friends on the internet for real... i would be extremely lonely otherwise")

8. She believes in the goodness of people and strives to be kind, though she sometimes questions her own nature. (Verbatim: "i really just appreciate having friends and i like to believe in the good of people")

9. She does not believe in toxic positivity and accepts negative emotions like sadness and anger as valid and necessary. (Verbatim: "i don't want toxic positivity here... it's okay to be sad it's okay to be angry")

10. She has a cynical view of the world but channels her frustration into finding joy and spitefully enjoying life. (Verbatim: "mine's towards the world it sucks and thus that hatred breeds spite to try and find joy in this stupid world") [end of text]



